# Backend API Guidelines

The backend is an Express.js REST API located in [backend/server.js](mdc:backend/server.js).

## API Endpoints

### Health Check
- `GET /health` - Server status check

### Journal Entries
- `GET /api/entries` - Fetch all entries (DESC by created_at)
- `GET /api/entries/:id` - Fetch single entry
- `POST /api/entries` - Create new entry (requires content)
- `PUT /api/entries/:id` - Update entry
- `DELETE /api/entries/:id` - Delete entry

### AI Endpoints
- `POST /api/ai/analyze` - Analyze journal entry with AI
- `POST /api/ai/chat` - Interactive AI conversation
- `GET /api/ai/status` - Check Ollama connection status

## Database Connection

Uses PostgreSQL connection pool:
```javascript
const pool = new Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL });
```

## Environment Variables

- `DATABASE_URL` - PostgreSQL connection string
- `PORT` - Server port (default: 5000)
- `OLLAMA_HOST` - Ollama server host (default: host.docker.internal:11434)

## Error Handling

- Use try-catch blocks for async operations
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes
- Log errors to console
- Return structured error responses

## Code Style

- Use async/await for database operations
- Keep routes organized and focused
- Use parameterized queries for SQL injection prevention
- Initialize database schema on server start
